e record on Benton County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids, July to August and August to September each came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years. In 2025 the middle saw July to August at 14% of normal and June to July at 37%. This year so far, May to June 2026 sits at 38% on the middle, and every grid had its driest year in 2013.</p>"}
